━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Model" means the K-AX Spartan AI model weights, parameters, tokenizer,
    configuration files, and any associated documentation provided by Licensor.

1.2 "Derivative Model" means any model created by fine-tuning, distilling,
    merging, quantizing, or otherwise modifying the Model.

1.3 "Output" means any content generated by running the Model or Derivative
    Model, including but not limited to text, code, and structured data.

1.4 "Commercial Use" means any use of the Model, Derivative Model, or Output
    that directly or indirectly generates revenue, including but not limited
    to: (a) integration into paid products or services; (b) use in internal
    business operations that contribute to revenue; (c) providing API access
    to third parties; (d) on-premise or cloud deployment for enterprise
    customers; (e) use in consulting or system integration services.

1.5 "Research Use" means use solely for academic research, personal learning,
    non-commercial evaluation, or benchmarking purposes, with results
    published openly and without commercial intent.

1.6 "Monthly Active Users" or "MAU" means the total number of unique users
    who interact with a service powered by the Model or Derivative Model
    within a calendar month.

